('eff3bed0-02d1-4e87-973d-2c19dbb86fea', 'f90fc22c-a15d-439e-8fde-5155de2762bf', 'assistant', '<think>\nOkay, I need to help the user create a simple motion design for their \"Hello World\" project using HyperFrames. Let me break down the requirements and figure out the best approach.\n\nFirst, the user wants a motion design that\'s simple. So, I should keep it straightforward without too many elements. The main focus will be on the \"Hello World\" text.\n\nI\'ll start by setting up the project structure. The root index.html needs to have a data-duration set to the total video length. The user mentioned a 5-second video, so that\'s what I\'ll use.\n\nNext, I\'ll create a composition for the intro scene. This will be in compositions/intro.html. The text \"Hello World\" should be centered, so I\'ll use Flexbox in CSS to achieve that. I\'ll choose a sans-serif font like Arial for simplicity and readability.\n\nFor the animation, I\'ll use CSS keyframes. I\'ll add an entrance animation where the text fades in and scales up. Then, a subtle bounce effect on the \'o\' in \"Hello\" to make it a bit more dynamic. The exit animation will fade the text out towards the end.\n\nI need to ensure that all timed elements have the required attributes: data-start, data-duration', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-14 18:37:24'),
