('4bfe8deb-2dd2-4583-8465-c77defc1c7f1', '822d5afd-9a73-48fa-a249-f1723489aae5', 'assistant', '{\"action\":\"create_motion\",\"project_name\":\"hello-world\",\"title\":\"Hello World Text Animation\",\"description\":\"A simple fade-in animation of Hello World text.\",\"visual_identity\":{\"primary\":\"#fff\",\"background\":\"#111\",\"text\":\"#fff\"},\"tasks\":[{\"action\":\"create_project\",\"label\":\"Initialize project\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"hello-world\"}},{\"action\":\"write_file\",\"label\":\"Write index.html\",\"params\":{\"path\":\"index.html\",\"content\":\"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\"><style>*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box} body{width:1920px;height:1080px;overflow:hidden;background:#111} .clip{position:absolute;opacity:0} @keyframes fadeIn{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)}to{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}}</style></head><body><div data-composition-id=\\\"main\\\" data-width=\\\"1920\\\" data-height=\\\"1080\\\" data-duration=\\\"5\\\" style=\\\"position:relative;width:1920px;height:1080px\\\"><div class=\\\"clip\\\" data-start=\\\"0\\\" data-duration=\\\"4\\\" data-track-index=\\\"0\\\" style=\\\"width:100%;height:100%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;animation:fadeIn 1s ease forwards\\\"><h1 style=\\\"color:#fff;font-size:80px;font-family:sans-serif\\\">Hello World</h1></div></div></body></html>\"},{\"action\":\"render\",\"label\":\"Render video\",\"params\":{\"output\":\"output.mp4\"}}]}', 'Alright, let me break down how I approached this problem. The user wants a simple \"Hello World\" motion design using the HyperFrames HTML template. They provided specific JSON structures and rules to follow, so my first step was to understand those requirements thoroughly.\n\nI started by identifying the necessary components. The project needs a JSON response with an action, project details, and tasks. The tasks include creating the project and writing the HTML file. The HTML must follow the exact structure provided, with specific data attributes and CSS animations.\n\nNext, I considered the project name. The user mentioned \"New Project\" with a slug, but since I\'m creating a new one, I chose \"hello-world\" as it\'s descriptive and fits the lowercase, hyphen-separated rule.\n\nFor the HTML content, I used the mandatory template. I set the body background to #111 for a dark theme, which is elegant and minimal. The clip element has a fadeIn animation starting at 0 seconds, lasting 1 second, with forwards fill mode so it stays visible.\n\nI made sure to include all required data attributes on the root div, ensuring the composition is correctly set up. The text is styled with a large font size and centered for a clean look. The clip\'s animation is defined using @keyframes, adhering to the rule against using JavaScript for animations.\n\nFinally, I structured the JSON response with the appropriate actions, labels, and parameters, ensuring it\'s self-contained and follows the user\'s guidelines precisely. This approach ensures the motion design is simple yet effective, meeting all specified criteria.', NULL, '2026-06-14 18:58:23'),
