('3ee3a2f4-6b61-4a85-8476-7317fd586cda', '0972f8cb-0180-460e-80e4-f20c5712d9e5', 'assistant', 'Motion design generated successfully. 3 tasks completed.', 'Okay, so the user wants me to create a motion design for a \"Hello World\" text. They mentioned it\'s for a new project, so I need to generate everything from scratch. Let me break down the requirements.\n\nFirst, the structure should be a JSON object with specific actions. Since it\'s a new project, I\'ll use the \"create_motion\" action. The project name needs to be in kebab-case, so I\'ll go with something like \"hello-world-123\" to make it unique.\n\nThe title and description are straightforward. I\'ll keep them simple and descriptive. For visual identity, the primary color is white, background is dark gray, and text is white to ensure good contrast.\n\nNext, the tasks. The first task is to create the project with the given name. Then, I need to write the HTML file. The template provided is essential, so I\'ll make sure to use it exactly as specified. The HTML includes a root div with specific data attributes and a clip div for the animation. I\'ll set the animation duration and timing to make the text fade in smoothly.\n\nI also need to ensure that the CSS uses keyframes for the fade-in effect and that the animation-fill-mode is set to forwards so the text stays visible after the animation. The text should be centered, so I\'ll use flexbox properties in the clip div.\n\nFinally, after writing the HTML, the last task is to render the video. I\'ll set the output to \"output.mp4\" as per the instructions.\n\nI should double-check that all the data attributes are correctly set and that the HTML structure matches the required template. Also, making sure that the colors and styling are consistent with the visual identity provided. Everything seems in order, so I can proceed to format the JSON response accordingly.', NULL, '2026-06-14 19:05:05'),
