('1f64a371-091b-48aa-a6fa-81f68cb7a874', '7c734177-03ad-42f8-accf-758a04c24454', 'user', 'cree moi un motion design de presentation de produit', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-14 19:22:07'),
('0aafa038-6c42-468b-8b55-3f3d41715d1e', '7c734177-03ad-42f8-accf-758a04c24454', 'assistant', 'Motion design generated successfully. 2 tasks completed.', 'Alright, let me break down how I approached creating the motion design for the product presentation.\n\nFirst, I needed to understand the user\'s request. They wanted a motion design for presenting a product, so I thought about the key elements that make such a presentation effective. Typically, this includes an engaging opening, clear product visuals, and a compelling call-to-action.\n\nI started by structuring the HTML according to the mandatory HyperFrames template. The root div had to include specific data attributes for composition ID, width, height, and duration. I set the duration to 8 seconds to allow enough time for all elements to animate smoothly without feeling rushed.\n\nNext, I considered the visual identity. The user didn\'t specify colors, so I chose a dark background (#0a0a0a) for a sleek look, white text for readability, and a vibrant accent color (#00ff88) to draw attention to the product and call-to-action.\n\nFor the tasks, I needed to create the project and write the HTML file. I made sure to include all necessary elements: a title, product image placeholder, features list, and a call-to-action button. Each element was placed within a clip div to enable animations.\n\nI planned the animations to guide the viewer\'s attention. The title fades in first, then the product image appears with a slight delay. The features list fades in next, and finally, the call-to-action button animates in. Each element has a staggered start time to create a smooth flow.\n\nI used CSS keyframes for the fadeIn animation, ensuring each clip has the forwards fill-mode so they remain visible after their animation completes. I also added a hover effect to the button for interactivity, even though it\'s a static HTML file.\n\nI made sure the HTML was self-contained, including all styles within the head section. This ensures that when the file is rendered, everything works without external dependencies.\n\nFinally, I reviewed the structure to ensure compliance with all rules: correct project name format, no external libraries, and all animations handled via keyframes. I also kept the design minimal and elegant, focusing on clarity and impact.', NULL, '2026-06-14 19:22:55'),
('afc163dd-d833-4a91-97b6-7395cec380d5', 'f935add9-b752-4870-906e-269de5de309d', 'user', 'cree moi un motion design de presentation de produit (cedrick agricolor) , cela devra etre tres realiste et professionnelle', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-14 19:43:14'),
('9a4dff21-e4a7-429a-a64e-c5fd86eca89e', 'f935add9-b752-4870-906e-269de5de309d', 'assistant', 'Motion design generated successfully. 3 tasks completed.', 'Okay, I need to help the user create a motion design for presenting Cedrick Agricolor\'s product. The user wants it to be very realistic and professional. Let me break down the steps.\n\nFirst, I\'ll start by understanding the structure required. The user provided a specific JSON format, so I need to make sure I follow that exactly. The main action here is \"create_motion\", so I\'ll structure the JSON accordingly.\n\nNext, the project name should be a kebab slug, so I\'ll use \"cedrick-agricolor\" as the project name. The title should be something clear, like \"Cedrick Agricolor Product Presentation\". The description needs to be concise, so I\'ll go with \"Professional product presentation for Cedrick Agricolor.\"\n\nFor the visual identity, I\'ll choose colors that convey professionalism and agriculture. A primary green (#4CAF50) seems fitting, a dark background (#1A232A) for contrast, and light text (#E5E7EB) for readability.\n\nNow, the tasks. The first task is to create the project with the given name. Then, I need to write the index.html file. The content should be the HyperFrames HTML template provided. I\'ll structure the HTML with the necessary elements and animations.\n\nIn the HTML, the root div has specific data attributes. I\'ll set the duration to 10 seconds for a longer presentation. Each clip will have its own start and duration times to create a smooth, sequential animation.\n\nI\'ll include multiple clips: a logo animation with a fade-in effect, a product shot with a slide-up animation, a close-up with a zoom-in, and a tagline that fades in after the product shots. Each animation uses keyframes for opacity and transform, ensuring they stay visible after finishing with animation-fill-mode: forwards.\n\nI\'ll make sure all the CSS is included within the style tag, and the body has the correct dimensions and background. The text elements will have appropriate styling for font size, family, and alignment.\n\nFinally, the last task is to render the video as output.mp4. I\'ll ensure all parameters are correctly set in the JSON so the rendering process goes smoothly.\n\nI need to double-check that the JSON structure is correct, with proper commas and brackets, and that all required fields are filled out. Also, the HTML content should be properly escaped and formatted within the JSON string.\n\nOverall, the goal is to create a polished, professional-looking motion design that effectively presents Cedrick Agricolor\'s product with realistic animations and a cohesive color scheme.', NULL, '2026-06-14 19:46:04'),
