for highlights, perhaps a bright blue. The font should be clean, like Inter.\n\nNow, the tasks. The first task is to create the project with the given name. Then, write the index.html file, which should include the necessary HTML structure with data attributes as per HyperFrames rules. Each element must be wrapped in a clip div with specific data attributes for start time, duration, and track index. The CSS should include keyframes for animations, ensuring smooth transitions and proper fill modes.\n\nI need to make sure that the HTML structure adheres strictly to the HyperFrames rules. The root composition div must have all the required data attributes. Every visible element must be inside a clip div with the correct styling and animations. The body should be set to the correct dimensions and overflow hidden.\n\nIn the HTML, I\'ll include the profile photo as an image asset. Since it\'s provided, I can reference it directly. The text elements will be styled with precise typography, using the specified font and colors. I\'ll use CSS for gradients, shadows, and other effects to enhance the visual appeal.\n\nThe animations should be smooth, with ease-in-out curves. I\'ll stagger the start times of different elements to create a dynamic flow. For example, the profile photo fades in first, followed by the name and title, then the skills, each with a slight delay to build the presentation.\n\nFinally, I\'ll ensure that the JSON response includes all necessary actions and parameters, correctly formatted without any markdown or extra text. The tasks should clearly outline the steps to initialize the project, write the HTML file, and render the output video.\n\nI think I\'ve covered all the requirements. Now, I\'ll structure the JSON response accordingly, making sure each part aligns with the guidelines and the user\'s request.', NULL, '2026-06-14 20:32:55'),
